## Recovery and source rulings

The compaction interruption did not reject implementation acceptance. On
recovery, canonical remains clean at the base above and the same native goal
is active. Partial root source is retained at `e1ebf9f`; independently authored
observer source continues from `e07de852`. No native or Kata effect was repeated.

Ruling: explicitly profile Python's installed startup files rather than admit a
site directory or change interpreter flags. Actual `sitecustomize.__file__` is
`/usr/lib/python3.11/sitecustomize.py`, resolving to
`/etc/python3.11/sitecustomize.py`. Both readonly profile executions must return
the same exact module name, observed alias, regular target and SHA256. The
raw helper source and command outputs, interpreter, flags, exit codes, dual
clocks and stdlib root are reopened before effects. A second alias to even the
same target refuses. This preserves the approved literal import closure and
records the machine's installed alias explicitly. Independent reader and root
fixture implementations share the data contract, never implementation code.

Root's42 private controls pass after observed alias/profile/static-binding
failures followed by corrections. These controls exercise exact-file admission,
retained raw command provenance, source mutations, wrong aliases, readiness,
fixed actor roles, kernel birth and failed-command retention. They are source
verification only; fresh-source independent review, actual profiles and live
E remain pending. Prior A/B/C/D UNKNOWN reports retain their original meaning.
